1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:05,053
Useful knowledge should stay with your team when a conversation ends.

2
00:00:05,053 --> 00:00:10,656
Company Memory gives your AI clients a shared place for selected decisions and results,

3
00:00:10,656 --> 00:00:13,058
with access controlled by your workspace.

4
00:00:14,658 --> 00:00:19,782
Start from Company Memory in your client's plugin catalogue and connect through the browser.

5
00:00:19,782 --> 00:00:24,906
Create a workspace, or join an existing one with an invitation link or code.

6
00:00:24,906 --> 00:00:27,834
This demo account already owns its shared memory.

7
00:00:29,434 --> 00:00:31,984
Each connected client has its own identity.

8
00:00:31,984 --> 00:00:36,354
You choose the memory, the zone, and the actions it may use.

9
00:00:36,354 --> 00:00:41,454
Signing in does not silently create another memory or give a client access to

10
00:00:41,454 --> 00:00:41,818
everything.

11
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:46,705
Here is a recorded result from the working pilot.

12
00:00:46,705 --> 00:00:51,087
A selected note about the fictional Aurora project entered the review queue.

13
00:00:51,087 --> 00:00:53,643
The server then confirmed accepted and visible.

14
00:00:53,643 --> 00:00:56,930
A queued request alone is never reported as saved.

15
00:00:58,530 --> 00:01:03,218
A separate read-only client retrieved that same note from the General zone.

16
00:01:03,218 --> 00:01:05,953
Both clients received the identical source hash.

17
00:01:05,953 --> 00:01:11,422
The knowledge belongs to the shared memory, so it does not depend on copying

18
00:01:11,422 --> 00:01:12,594
the previous conversation.

19
00:01:14,194 --> 00:01:19,116
The read-only client could retrieve the note, but its attempt to submit a new

20
00:01:19,116 --> 00:01:20,171
one was denied.

21
00:01:20,171 --> 00:01:23,335
A request to an unapproved memory was also denied.

22
00:01:23,335 --> 00:01:27,202
These checks used an isolated test account, with no corporate records.

23
00:01:28,802 --> 00:01:34,718
Disconnecting the reviewer client removed its access immediately, even while its token was still

24
00:01:34,718 --> 00:01:35,140
valid.

25
00:01:35,140 --> 00:01:39,366
The writer stayed connected and retrieved the same source afterward.

26
00:01:39,366 --> 00:01:42,746
Shared knowledge and other approved clients remained available.

27
00:01:44,346 --> 00:01:48,666
Company Memory keeps selected knowledge available across approved clients.

28
00:01:48,666 --> 00:01:54,906
This walkthrough uses real portal screens and recorded pilot results with synthetic data.

29
00:01:54,906 --> 00:02:00,666
Free and paid accounts use the same explicit connection and permission model.